check=second-pass-mutates-nothing
operator=guard-deletion
target=pb/pb/prereqs.py
mutation=replace | pb/pb/prereqs.py | for name in ("kubectl", "kind"):\n        if first_executable(candidates[name]) is not None:\n            continue\n        record = resolved(name) | for name in ("kubectl", "kind"):\n        record = resolved(name)
statement=Delete the probe-first guard on the two acquired cluster tools, so every pass
statement=re-acquires them whether or not they are already present. The run still converges
statement=and still probes, so only the idempotence property breaks: the second pass now
statement=carries a mutation, and an ensure that mutates on a converged host is the failure
statement=the replay exists to refuse.
